{
  "item": "ArmorMale30",
  "mu_name": "Dragon Knight Armor",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain loads MODEL_DRAGON_KNIGHT_* from Data/Player/HDK_ArmorMale01.bmd (ZzzOpenData.cpp:222-230; the helm is HDK_HelmMale 1). MU's group 8 number 29. Ours is named ArmorMale30 by the index-plus-one rule every other set keeps: MU never loads a *Male30 file, so nothing collides, and the set tooling groups it by its Helm/Armor/... prefix.",
  "why_this_one": "The Blade Knight's level-380 set, Kanturu's gear (the user, 2026-10-22: 'we need to work on missing weapons and armors', then the four 380 sets and their weapons first, built on main and dormant until Kanturu drops them).",
  "profile": "armour",
  "stats": {
    "note": "The item's own row: OpenMU's Season 6 initialiser (Season 2's level-380 sets; 0.75 and 0.95d have none).",
    "from": "openmu/src/Persistence/Initialization/VersionSeasonSix/Items/Armors.cs:146.",
    "call": "CreateArmor(29, 3, 2, 3, \"Dragon Knight Armor\", 140, 88, 90, 380, 170, 60, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)",
    "group": 8,
    "number": 29,
    "drop_level": 140,
    "drops_from_monsters": true,
    "drops_from_monsters_note": "Drops in Kanturu only (the user, 2026-10-25: \"The 380 gear\", \"Kanturu only\"): sim::kanturuGear keeps anything asking level 380 to the maps whose rules drop kanturu_gear. Its drop level is MU's.",
    "slot": 3,
    "width": 2,
    "height": 3,
    "defense": 88,
    "durability": 90,
    "requires": {
      "level": 380,
      "strength": 170,
      "agility": 60,
      "energy": 0,
      "vitality": 0
    },
    "requires_note": "MU asks level 380 (OpenMU's levelRequirement), and so does ours (the user, 2026-10-25: \"Level 380\"): found in the Ruins from 320, worn from 380. The stat columns are raw, scaled by the drop level as every item's.",
    "classes": [
      "knight"
    ],
    "class_level": 2,
    "class_level_note": "The Blade Knight's alone: OpenMU's darkKnightClassLevel 2, not the third class. sim::fits asks Wearer::second (docs/game/second-class-gear.md)."
  },
  "sheets": {
